RoboBuddy IDE — multi-license repository

There is no single license that applies to every file in this repository.

1. Original RoboBuddy IDE source code is licensed under the MIT License unless a file or directory states otherwise. The MIT text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

2. Third-party software, source-derived parameters, runtime distributions, model files, policies, and generated derivatives retain the licenses and notices stated in their source directories, manifests, or THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

3. MicroDuck 3D model and collision files copied from pollen-robotics/microduck_rl are NOT covered by the RoboBuddy MIT grant. Upstream declares its 3D model files as “Creative Commons BY-SA-NC”. The upstream declaration does not specify a Creative Commons license version, so RoboBuddy does not assign or imply one. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and models/microduck/source/.

4. Some existing locally generated MicroDuck artifacts are marked PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0 in assets/microduck/manifest.json. Those file-level declarations remain controlling for those artifacts.

When redistributing a subset of this repository, comply with the license that applies to every included component.

Asimov 1 source-derived model and visual assets under models/asimov/ are separately
licensed under the upstream CERN-OHL-S-2.0 hardware / GPL-2.0 software notices.
See models/asimov/source/HARDWARE-LICENSE.txt, SOFTWARE-LICENSE.txt and
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. They are not covered by the original-code MIT grant.
